      "title": "Ask HN: Local AI product situation",
      "summary": "Right now it seems every company wants you to buy their fancy new expensive computer to run local AI models. Why would we want to buy a whole new computer to run local AI models? Why not create a device which has its own memory and chip designed specifically to run models and it plugs into your existing computer thunderbolt port (or event USB 3.2 as loading the model is one time process).",
      "summary_html": "<p>Right now it seems every company wants you to buy their fancy new expensive computer to run local AI models. Why would we want to buy a whole new computer to run local AI models? Why not create a device which has its own memory and chip designed specifically to run models and it plugs into your existing computer thunderbolt port (or event USB 3.2 as loading the model is one time process).</p>\n\n<p>Comments URL: <a href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50129150\">https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50129150</a></p>\n<p>Points: 1</p>\n<p># Comments: 0</p>",
